From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BeagleBone Black Driver Project <embedded@example.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] bbb: enable peripheral support

Enable the kernel subsystems required for the BeagleBone Black
all-peripheral device driver development project.

The configuration enables support for:

- GPIO
- I2C
- SPI
- UART
- PWM
- CAN
- IIO/ADC
- Device Tree
- Kernel modules
- Kernel debugging

This patch provides the base kernel configuration required before
developing and testing individual peripheral drivers.

Signed-off-by: BeagleBone Black Driver Project <embedded@example.com>
---
 kernel/configs/bbb_driver_defconfig | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/configs/bbb_driver_defconfig b/kernel/configs/bbb_driver_defconfig
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..111111111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kernel/configs/bbb_driver_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+#
+# BeagleBone Black Device Driver Project
+#
+
+# Architecture
+CONFIG_ARM=y
+CONFIG_ARCH_MULTI_V7=y
+CONFIG_ARCH_OMAP2PLUS=y
+CONFIG_SOC_AM33XX=y
+
+# Device Tree
+CONFIG_OF=y
+CONFIG_OF_FLATTREE=y
+
+# Device Management
+CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
+CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
+
+# GPIO
+CONFIG_GPIOLIB=y
+
+# I2C
+CONFIG_I2C=y
+CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=y
+
+# SPI
+CONFIG_SPI=y
+CONFIG_SPI_MASTER=y
+CONFIG_SPI_SPIDEV=y
+
+# UART
+CONFIG_TTY=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_8250=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y
+
+# PWM
+CONFIG_PWM=y
+
+# CAN
+CONFIG_CAN=y
+CONFIG_CAN_RAW=y
+CONFIG_CAN_DEV=y
+
+# ADC / Industrial I/O
+CONFIG_IIO=y
+
+# Networking / SocketCAN
+CONFIG_NET=y
+CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
+CONFIG_INET=y
+
+# Kernel Modules
+CONFIG_MODULES=y
+CONFIG_MODULE_UNLOAD=y
+
+# Debugging
+CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
+CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y
+CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
-- 
